  "notes": "DUAL USAGE:\n1. GROWTH: Describes untidy, overgrown vegetation or hair\n2. FIRE: Describes fierce, roaring flames\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {草|くさ}がぼうぼう: grass has grown wild\n- {髭|ひげ}がぼうぼう: unkempt beard\n- {髪|かみ}がぼうぼう: disheveled hair\n- {火|ひ}がぼうぼう: blazing fire\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ぼさぼさ: messy, disheveled (hair)\n- めらめら: flames flickering\n- ごうごう: roaring (fire, water)",
